> > Would .i ki'e ba lenu work? (As in 'Thanks before the event'?)
> 
> "ki'e ba lenu" isn't valid. The "nu" requires a bridi after it.
> Also, the "ba" and the "ki'e" don't connect in any way. The
> best interpretation of that is "Thanks, future event of <omitted>"

How about .i le bavfau cu selckire ? ('The future event is receiving
gratitude.' (jbofi'e didn't recgnize 'bavfau' which is the rafsi for bavli
'future' and fasnu 'event', and ckire's rafsi is unusable (unless there's one
besides 'kir')), but otherwise it seems to work. Also, it seems ki'e is a rafsi
for 'cushion', which definitely doesn't help.))

